invariant: INV-26
file: quic_keys.c
catches: quic_suite_test
reason: a host object stores the AES header protection key's schedule at
  AES-128's 16 bytes under every AES suite, so a TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384
  connection masks its packet numbers with half its "quic hp" key. RFC
  9001 section 5.4.3 runs header protection with the AEAD's own AES,
  AES-256 there, so the peer computes another mask and every Handshake
  and 1-RTT packet fails to unprotect. quic_suite_test, a host binary,
  compares an AES-256 packet byte for byte with an independent
  computation.

--- old
        aes_traffic_key_store(h->schedule, h->key, suite_key_len(suite));
--- new
        aes_traffic_key_store(h->schedule, h->key, AES_128_KEY);
